// A ROLL AND A MESSAGE WERE MISSING FROM BOTH, and that is because the Fishing Trawler awards its
// catch directly rather than rolling for it - so until the Wilderness spot there was nothing to
// roll with. The xp is Old School's and unchanged.
//
// THE RATES ARE THE SHARK'S, NOT BETTER. success_low 3 / success_high 40 is exactly what
// fishing_struct_shark carries, so a Wilderness manta is caught no faster than a shark is - the
// spot pays more per catch because the fish are worth more, not because the rolls are kinder. The
// assessment document's argument for #10 was that a risky spot which simply out-earns the Trawler
// replaces it rather than adding to it; this is what keeps it a sidegrade.
[fishing_struct_mantaray]
param=productexp,690
param=productmessage,You catch a manta ray.
param=success_low,3
param=success_high,40
param=fishing_pet_base,0

[fishing_struct_seaturtle]
param=productexp,570
param=productmessage,You catch a sea turtle.
param=success_low,3
param=success_high,40
param=fishing_pet_base,0

// THE TWO EELS AND THE FROG SPAWN, which the maps have had spots for since the 377 import and
// nothing behind them: three spot types in Mort Myre with Bait and two in the Lumbridge Swamp
// Caves with Net and Bait, at nineteen spawn points, none of which answered a click.
// skill_fishing/scripts/fishing_spots/slimeyeel.rs2 and cavefish.rs2 have the two handlers and
// where each number comes from.
//
// THE RATES ARE THE WIKI'S OWN PAIRS, not a guess from a chart. Every fish page carries a
// {{Skilling success chart}} whose low= and high= are the game's own stat_random arguments, and
// those are what these are: raw slimy eel and raw cave eel share low=10 high=80 (one chart, two
// series, cascade=yes - which is the same thing as fish2-then-fish1 in ~fish_roll), and frog spawn
// is low=16 high=96. The engine's formula is floor(low*(99-L)/98) + floor(high*(L-1)/98) + 1 out
// of 256, so frog spawn works out at 16.8% a roll at level 33 and 37.9% at 99, which is exactly
// what the wiki's chart plots.
[fishing_struct_mort_slimey_eel]
// 65 and not 80: a slimy eel is worth 80 experience in the Lumbridge Swamp Caves and 65 in Mort
// Myre, and this obj is caught in both. The struct carries Mort Myre's number - where seventeen of
// the nineteen spawn points are, and what the obj is named for - and cavefish.rs2 tops up the
// difference when one comes out of the caves.
param=productexp,650
param=productmessage,You catch a slimy eel.
param=success_low,10
param=success_high,80
param=fishing_pet_base,0

[fishing_struct_raw_cave_eel]
param=productexp,800
param=productmessage,You catch a cave eel.
param=success_low,10
param=success_high,80
// the one of the three the Heron table does list
param=fishing_pet_base,257770

[fishing_struct_giant_frogspawn]
// "Frog spawn" is this obj's own name - the cache calls it giant_frogspawn and the gourmet impling
// already hands it out (skill_hunter/scripts/hunter_implings_loot.rs2), which is where it came from
// until now.
param=productexp,750
param=productmessage,You catch some frog spawn.
param=success_low,16
param=success_high,96
param=fishing_pet_base,0

// THE KARAMBWAN, whose numbers were mine and are now the wiki's. The catch itself lives in
// quests/quest_tbwt/scripts/quest_tbwt.rs2 (the vessel dropped by hand) and is reached from
// skill_fishing/scripts/fishing_spots/karambwan.rs2 (the spot clicked) - two doors, one roll - and
// it is the one fish here that cannot go through ~fish_roll, because a karambwan takes the
// karambwanji whether or not it is caught and ~fish_roll deletes bait only on a catch. So the
// struct holds the numbers and that label reads them out of it.
//
// 50 experience and low=5 high=160 at 65, which is Old School's published pair and the same source
// every other struct in this file is built from. The original 2004 value was 105 and RuneScape 3
// still pays it; this build has followed Old School everywhere else it had the choice - cooking one
// thoroughly already pays Old School's 190 - so it follows it here.
[fishing_struct_tbwt_raw_karambwan]
param=productexp,500
param=productmessage,Something heavy goes into the vessel and does not come out again. You do not look too closely.
param=success_low,5
param=success_high,160
param=fishing_pet_base,170874
